 ## Background
-This method was introduced in the context of compressed random-access trees for spatially coherent data [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the issue that subtrees in a mipmap tree may extend beyond the defined domain, resulting in residual blocks with undefined values [S1, unofficial]. The approach leverages the known property that $k$-means can be extended to partially defined data while preserving convergence [LFWV03, cited in S1, unofficial]. It is used in conjunction with brood-based vector quantization to compress 3D data [S1, unofficial].
